{
 "flight": "STS-134",
 "notes": "STS-134's own I-loads in G2 (GNC OPS 2) for rendezvous and proximity operations: every word of the orbit-targeting (#PCGZ*, #DGW*), relative-navigation (#PCGN*, #DGL*), and flight-control/DAP mass-property and gain (#DGCQORB, #DGC1ORB, #DGC9ORB, #PCGCFL2, #PCGCFL3, #PCGCCOM) csects that the flight's load changed from the load module. Source: the PATCH SUMMARY of PFS/mafgen/DASS_G2.ASC, the MAFGEN listing of STS-134's own GNC2 load ('STS134/OI034/C2 MDD 134.09 DASS GNC2', 13 Dec 2010): 'was' is its LM column (the load module, what this tape holds), H its MM column (the flight's); corrected-G2.fcm, the flown G2 dump, holds the MM value in every cell. PASS-IDLE independently sent flown values from the DASS G2 dump (pure-G2.fcm), 2026-10-09: CGZB_LAMB_ILOAD, the GLQREN locals, and STS-134's nominal c.g. and inertia in #DGCQORB (CGCS_CG_NOM 1104.2, 0.4, 371.8 in; CGCS_MOMENTS_OF_INERTIA_NOM 938131, 7129268, 7462045 slug-ft^2; CGCS_PRODUCTS_OF_INERTIA_NOM -2415, 273803, -2486; the tape's are 1105.2, 0.4, 376.2; 951736, 7180436, 7507857; -2475.2, 274960, -2538.9) -- all agree with these cells, except that PASS-IDLE listed the Lambert flags 28 and up OFF, where both DASS files have 29-40 ON (28 OFF); sets 29-40 are not used by STS-134's rendezvous. CGZB_LAMB_ILOAD's set 7 (X'0E354') and CGZV_ROFF_ILOAD_ARRAY+97 (X'0E02D') are among 54 summary lines printed with a '0' carriage control in column 1, which the first version of this spec missed; the rendezvous ones are in. Left out on purpose: #PCGRRMC CGRS_JET_MAP and CGRV_FDI_TOLERANCE (the flight's jet map swaps logical jet numbers; vehdyn's jet decoding has not been checked against it), the VRCS leak-temperature limits (#DGRRRCS) and CGRS_DILEMMA_CTR_LIMIT (#DGR8RCS) -- RCS redundancy management; and the rest of the GNC compools (#PCGGCOM, #PCGCMFR, ... about 1900 words), not reviewed. Positions: 'flat' (volume data halfwords) in each csect's G2 copy -- the csect's offset on the volume found from distinctive runs of its own halfwords; where several configurations carry the csect, the copy agreeing best with an OPS 2 memory image (rr-run2/sts134r-ipl) over +/-2048 halfwords; each cell confirmed ('was' there, and at least 48 of the 80 surrounding halfwords agreeing). Only the G2 copy is changed: STS-134's G1/G6 load (DASS_G16.ASC) has other values for 27 of #DGLJRCV's words and 7 of #PCGNFLT's, so other configurations' copies are left alone (the first version changed all four #DGLJRCV copies). Not placed, so not on the volume: CGCS_NUM_FILTERS (two cells), CGPS_CRHCRA+1, CGPS_CRHCPA+1, CGNS_T_GPS_CYCLE, CGNS_KFACTOR, CGNS_MEAS_THRESHOLD+1, five #PCGNREM GPS antenna boresight cells. RENDEZVOUS_PLAN.md 5e.",
